+The viewer's context menu includes 3D. Alt+Shift+3 opens it directly. Its "3D
+Input Format" entry is the stereo layer's own menu: choose the input packing of a
+photograph (every packing, in either order), Not 3D, or swap its left and right
+eyes. That choice is the photograph's: it is kept in the layer's per-file store,
+which the file manager, the thumbnailers and the other viewers read, so the
+photograph shows the same everywhere, and it follows the photograph when a
+program renames or moves it. The file itself is never changed, unless you choose
+"Save the correction into the file". Below it are the viewer's own views, for
+the session, as before: Stereo, either eye alone, and Not 3D for every
+photograph (Alt+Shift+D, L, O and N). Alt+Shift+W swaps the eyes of the
+photograph shown.
 
 Anaglyph photographs can be converted to side by side. The colour is reconstructed
 and approximate because an anaglyph retains only part of each eye's colour. A
